{"kind": "journal", "text": "Approach: batch 1 broad scan of all feature families showed negative momentum SRs at 20-120d and positive ma(n) meaning medium-long horizon mean reversion. Batch 2-3 refined vol-scaled reversal and uncovered an echo: the 120d return delayed 120d predicts positively (SR 1.04) while recent 120d return predicts negatively, and they are additive. Batch 4-5 mapped a clean cycle break at lag 120: delay(ret(n),120) positive for all n, ret(n) negative, delay(ret(120),60) is zero, delay(ret(120),250) is flat-negative. Best compact form is ret(250) minus 2x ret(120), i.e. long the old window t-250 to t-120 minus recent window t-120 to t, train SR 1.93, IC 0.012. Batch 6 robustness: SR plateau 1.86-1.95 across all vol scalings and component-z forms, decays gracefully with extra lag (1.49-1.76 at 3-10d), so the effect is not fragile. Beta(250) adds IC but hurts portfolio SR in every blend, so dropped. Reporting three structurally different implementations of the one dominant factor rather than weaker diversifiers (MA crossover 1.0, beta 0.5) to maximize expected OOS Sharpe; stopping after 6 of 12 batches to avoid selection overfit on train noise.", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:32:19.764925+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["sub(ret(250), add(ret(120), ret(120)))", "div(sub(ret(250), add(ret(120), ret(120))), std(40))", "div(sub(ret(250), add(ret(120), ret(120))), std(120))"], "chosen_sr_train": [1.9261, 1.9511, 1.8904], "rationale": "Panel exhibits a dominant cyclical mean-reversion factor with a clean break at lag 120: returns over t-250 to t-120 predict positively while returns over t-120 to t predict negatively, and the legs are additive. The compact form ret(250) minus 2x ret(120) captures both legs with equal weight (train SR 1.93, IC 0.012) and sits on a broad robustness plateau: SR 1.86-1.95 across every vol-scaling denominator, component-z and ensemble variants, and it decays gracefully under extra implementation lag. Reporting the raw form plus two vol-scaled variants (std 40 and std 120 denominators) as structurally hedged implementations of the same well-identified factor; weaker independent families (MA crossover, beta, corrm) were tested and excluded because every blend diluted portfolio Sharpe.", "n_batches_used": 6, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:32:27.091637+00:00"}
